==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:viage}}
From {{inh|en|enm|viage}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|viage}} and {{der|en|fro|voiage}}, from {{der|en|la|viaticum}}. The modern spelling is under the influence of Modern {{der|en|fr|voyage}}. {{doublet|en|viaticum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvɔɪ.ɪd͡ʒ/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvojɪd͡ʒ/|a=SSB}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-voyage.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvaɪd͡ʒ/|aa=<<obsolete>>, <<nonstandard>>|ref={{R:en:Hurd:1847|Voyage|3|90}}}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A long [[journey#Noun|journey]], especially by [[ship#Noun|ship]].
#: {{ux|en|He went on a '''voyage''' to France.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Julius Caesar|act=IV|scene=iii|page=126|column=1|passage=There is a Tide in the affayres of men, / Which taken at the Flood, leades on to Fortune: / Omitted, all the '''voyage''' of their life, / Is bound in Shallowes, and in Miſeries.}}
#* {{RQ:Beaumont Fletcher Comedies and Tragedies|folio=2nd|title=The Wild-Goose Chase|act=V|scene=vi|page=467|column=2|passage=I love a Sea '''voyage''' and a bluſtring tempeſt; [...]}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A [[written]] [[account]] of a journey or [[travel]].
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=[[s:A Full and True Relation of the Great and Wonderful Revolution That Hapned Lately in the Kingdom of Siam in the East-Indies/Preface|The Preface to the Reader]]|year=1690|page=v|location=London|publisher=Randal Taylor|text=I cannot learn what his Name was, unleſs by the Inſcription of the Letters he ſent to the Pope, and to the French King in the Year 1688, mentioned in the ſecond '''Voyage''' of Father Tachard {{...}}|title=A Full and True Relation of the Great and Wonderful Revolution That Hapned Lately in the Kingdom of Siam in the East-Indies}}
#* {{quote-book|en|chapter=[[s:A Full and True Relation of the Great and Wonderful Revolution That Hapned Lately in the Kingdom of Siam in the East-Indies/Part 1|A Relation of the Late Great Revolution in Siam, and the Driving Out of the French]]|year=1690|page=1|location=London|publisher=Randal Taylor|text=By the various Relations, Embaſſies and '''Voyages''' of Siam that have been publiſht within theſe laſt Four Years {{...}}|title=A Full and True Relation of the Great and Wonderful Revolution That Hapned Lately in the Kingdom of Siam in the East-Indies}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The [[act#Noun|act]] or [[practice#Noun|practice]] of [[travelling#Noun|travelling]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon New Atlantis|page=12|passage=[...] [A]ll Nations haue [[interknowledge|Enterknowledge]] one of another, either by '''Voyage''' into Forreine Parts, or by Strangers that come to them: [...]}}

